-- title:
--   G Hat Sandwich Sum Last Eq Prefix
-- statement:
--   **Summing the last G-hat outcome collapses the sandwich to the prefix.**
--   Write $g_{\le i}$ for the completed outcome prefix through coordinate $i$.
--   Let `params` have a field model, let `family` be an indexed polynomial family, let `n` be a natural number, let `xs` be a point tuple of length `n+1`, and let `gsPrefix` be a completed outcome tuple of length `n`. Split a length-`n+1` outcome tuple into this prefix and a final outcome using `gHatTupleOutcomePrefixLastEquiv`. Then
--
--   $$
--   \begin{aligned}
--   &\sum_{g}\operatorname{gHatHalfProductOutcomeOperator}\!\left(\mathrm{params},\mathrm{family},n+1,xs,
--   \operatorname{prefixLast}^{-1}(g_{\le i},g)\right)
--   \operatorname{gHatHalfProductOutcomeOperator}\!\left(\mathrm{params},\mathrm{family},n+1,xs,
--   \operatorname{prefixLast}^{-1}(g_{\le i},g)\right)^{\dagger}\\
--   &=T\,T^{\dagger},
--   \end{aligned}
--   $$
--
--   where `T` is the length-`n` half-product on the truncated point tuple and `gsPrefix`. The result is the finite outcome-sum collapse used at the endpoint of the line one-point sandwich argument.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.gHatSandwich_sum_last_eq_prefix`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/LionSR/MIPStarRE/blob/f382c801026f53a9efc260fdee707cb35e0adb15/MIPStarRE/LDT/Pasting/ComparisonLemmas/LdSandwichLineOnePoint/PrefixMoved.lean#L181-L248

